  "summary": "This convenience-focused Mexican recipe features a rich <b>poblano tortilla bake</b> that can be fully assembled a day before serving. Layers of flash-fried corn tortillas, tender black beans, and smoky charred poblano strips are bathed in a tangy <b>salsa verde</b> and smothered with meltable Oaxaca cheese. By allowing the assembled casserole to rest overnight in the refrigerator, the tortillas absorb the aromatic spices and savory juices from the salsa and beans, producing an extraordinarily cohesive and flavorful texture once baked. Ideal for stress-free entertaining or busy weeknights, this hearty dish transitions seamlessly from fridge to oven. When baked to bubbling perfection, the top layer of <b>shredded cheese</b> forms a golden crust that contrasts deliciously with the soft, comforting layers underneath. Serve hot garnished with chopped cilantro, diced avocado, and a dollop of Mexican crema for an authentic fiesta-ready meal that requires zero last-minute prep work.",
